  "caveats": [
    "Pure combinatorial integer arithmetic — no symbolic-q, no floats.  The per-factor pole assignment uses the leading-order behaviour at q → 0 (max of σ-part and d·I-part).  For the crystal limit to be accurate the h-coefficient d must be proportional to h = q − q⁻¹; set h_is_d_proportional=False if you have non-h constant d's (none in canonical atomic braids).",
    "Enumerating SYTs scales as Σ_λ |SYT(λ)| = n!.  At A=6 this is 18! ≈ 6.4·10¹⁵ — intractable.  Practical approach: restrict to the column-rich maximizer λ* = (1^n) per audit Step 3, OR use crystal_basis.py's Demazure sub-crystal enumeration.  Current script does full enumeration for A ≤ 4 only as a correctness check."
  ]
